WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.110 --> 00:00:03.119
I've lost more of

00:00:03.120 --> 00:00:04.589
my partner nation brothers than I

00:00:04.590 --> 00:00:05.909
have on my U.S.

00:00:05.910 --> 00:00:06.910
side.

00:00:08.070 --> 00:00:09.150
I've buried all of them.

00:00:10.960 --> 00:00:12.459
They would put their lives in front

00:00:12.460 --> 00:00:13.749
of mine, and I would do the same for

00:00:13.750 --> 00:00:14.750
them.

00:00:17.600 --> 00:00:18.739
And that's going to continue for the

00:00:18.740 --> 00:00:19.740
rest of my life.

00:00:26.940 --> 00:00:28.405
The nightmare scenario of...

00:00:28.406 --> 00:00:29.317
Desperation engulfed...

00:00:29.318 --> 00:00:30.031
Panic at the airport...

00:00:30.032 --> 00:00:31.919
Desperate people pour onto the

00:00:31.920 --> 00:00:32.158
run...

00:00:32.159 --> 00:00:33.688
Confirm an explosion

00:00:33.689 --> 00:00:34.649
Chances of getting on them are
growing

00:00:34.650 --> 00:00:35.629
slimmer and slimmer.

00:00:35.630 --> 00:00:37.259
My national security team and I have

00:00:37.260 --> 00:00:38.609
been closely monitoring the

00:00:38.610 --> 00:00:39.719
situation on the ground in

00:00:39.720 --> 00:00:40.769
Afghanistan.

00:00:40.770 --> 00:00:42.599
The truth is, this did

00:00:42.600 --> 00:00:44.549
unfold more quickly than

00:00:44.550 --> 00:00:46.349
we had anticipated

00:00:46.350 --> 00:00:48.399
In August of 2021 as the U.S.

00:00:48.400 --> 00:00:49.379
government pulled out of

00:00:49.380 --> 00:00:51.209
Afghanistan, Air Force veteran

00:00:51.210 --> 00:00:53.069
Travis Petersen decided to go back

00:00:53.070 --> 00:00:54.809
into the country on his own.

00:00:54.810 --> 00:00:56.609
While everybody is trying to leave

00:00:56.610 --> 00:00:57.659
Afghanistan.

00:00:57.660 --> 00:00:58.532
I'm trying to get back into.

00:00:58.533 --> 00:00:59.159
OK.

00:00:59.160 --> 00:01:01.949
Yes. Before I knew it, I was

00:01:01.950 --> 00:01:03.629
jumping on an airplane.

00:01:03.630 --> 00:01:05.549
I had no idea what was

00:01:05.550 --> 00:01:06.599
going to happen after that.

00:01:07.620 --> 00:01:09.329
Peterson, who served two years in

00:01:09.330 --> 00:01:11.489
Iraq and 10 years in Afghanistan,

00:01:11.490 --> 00:01:13.319
wanted to help the men and women he

00:01:13.320 --> 00:01:15.269
had worked with and fought with to

00:01:15.270 --> 00:01:16.469
escape.

00:01:16.470 --> 00:01:18.089
Afghans who had partnered with the

00:01:18.090 --> 00:01:19.829
U.S. government during the 20 year

00:01:19.830 --> 00:01:21.689
occupation could be eligible

00:01:21.690 --> 00:01:23.609
for special immigrant visas

00:01:23.610 --> 00:01:24.629
or SIV's.

00:01:25.650 --> 00:01:28.019
So for your special operation guys,

00:01:28.020 --> 00:01:29.969
why do you think that the U.S.

00:01:29.970 --> 00:01:32.519
is obligated to bring them

00:01:32.520 --> 00:01:33.959
here? Because that's what you've

00:01:33.960 --> 00:01:34.469
been doing.

00:01:34.470 --> 00:01:36.389
Yes, there's a huge obligation

00:01:36.390 --> 00:01:37.649
to bring them here.

00:01:37.650 --> 00:01:39.119
I wouldn't be alive if it wasn't for

00:01:39.120 --> 00:01:41.489
these guys. There's a thousand

00:01:41.490 --> 00:01:43.319
other individuals just like me that

00:01:43.320 --> 00:01:45.479
wouldn't be alive because

00:01:45.480 --> 00:01:47.339
of the intelligence

00:01:47.340 --> 00:01:48.959
on the battlefield as well of

00:01:48.960 --> 00:01:50.549
putting themselves in front of me.

00:01:50.550 --> 00:01:53.009
There's numerous occasions where

00:01:53.010 --> 00:01:54.179
they would yell at me for getting

00:01:54.180 --> 00:01:55.559
off the helicopter to go grab

00:01:55.560 --> 00:01:57.179
somebody because they knew it was a

00:01:57.180 --> 00:01:59.699
bad situation, or

00:01:59.700 --> 00:02:01.589
they would surround me and

00:02:01.590 --> 00:02:03.419
it would encircle me as I

00:02:03.420 --> 00:02:04.420
was going to move to get to somebody.

00:02:07.310 --> 00:02:09.019
Eventually, Peterson would connect

00:02:09.020 --> 00:02:10.549
with a group of other veterans,

00:02:10.550 --> 00:02:12.439
private citizens, active duty

00:02:12.440 --> 00:02:14.269
military and philanthropists

00:02:14.270 --> 00:02:16.069
who had also decided to take matters

00:02:16.070 --> 00:02:17.569
into their own hands.

00:02:17.570 --> 00:02:19.519
It just became this massive push

00:02:19.520 --> 00:02:20.520
to get these guys out.

00:02:21.560 --> 00:02:23.119
Many of these individuals were

00:02:23.120 --> 00:02:25.339
members of Afghan special operations

00:02:25.340 --> 00:02:27.199
units trained and funded by

00:02:27.200 --> 00:02:28.789
the American military.

00:02:28.790 --> 00:02:30.649
They participated in direct combat

00:02:30.650 --> 00:02:32.119
against the Taliban and are

00:02:32.120 --> 00:02:33.619
currently in hiding because their

00:02:33.620 --> 00:02:34.669
lives are in danger

00:02:35.750 --> 00:02:36.979
because they weren't directly

00:02:36.980 --> 00:02:38.989
employed by the American military.

00:02:38.990 --> 00:02:40.189
The State Department hasn't

00:02:40.190 --> 00:02:41.539
evacuated them.

00:02:41.540 --> 00:02:43.399
We've talked about how most

00:02:43.400 --> 00:02:45.229
of these guys took on missions in

00:02:45.230 --> 00:02:47.239
collaboration with the U.S.

00:02:47.240 --> 00:02:48.739
government. You have been training

00:02:48.740 --> 00:02:50.209
around this whole time.

00:02:50.210 --> 00:02:51.079
You know why?

00:02:51.080 --> 00:02:52.969
Why did you have to do this

00:02:52.970 --> 00:02:54.119
as a private effort?

00:02:54.120 --> 00:02:55.159
Where is the U.S.

00:02:55.160 --> 00:02:56.389
government in this?

00:02:56.390 --> 00:02:57.979
It's different with the Soviet

00:02:57.980 --> 00:02:59.809
process with interpreters

00:02:59.810 --> 00:03:01.549
because they worked for an entity.

00:03:01.550 --> 00:03:04.009
They worked for a company.

00:03:04.010 --> 00:03:05.389
My guys didn't, they worked for the

00:03:05.390 --> 00:03:06.559
Afghan military.

00:03:06.560 --> 00:03:08.389
If we could just re designate these

00:03:08.390 --> 00:03:10.279
guys as being

00:03:10.280 --> 00:03:12.229
SIV or on a humanitarian

00:03:12.230 --> 00:03:14.149
parole, we could have them out

00:03:14.150 --> 00:03:15.499
today.

00:03:15.500 --> 00:03:17.329
During that chaotic week following

00:03:17.330 --> 00:03:19.009
the U.S. withdrawal, Peterson

00:03:19.010 --> 00:03:20.749
physically extracted some of the men

00:03:20.750 --> 00:03:22.399
he had worked with, picking them out

00:03:22.400 --> 00:03:23.599
of the crowd.

00:03:23.600 --> 00:03:25.099
He escorted them to a security

00:03:25.100 --> 00:03:26.779
checkpoint at the airport and

00:03:26.780 --> 00:03:28.639
verified their identities

00:03:28.640 --> 00:03:29.849
through private donations.

00:03:29.850 --> 00:03:31.639
He arranged for four flights out of

00:03:31.640 --> 00:03:34.459
Afghanistan over a two week period.

00:03:34.460 --> 00:03:36.319
Peterson was at the airport in Kabul

00:03:36.320 --> 00:03:38.299
on the day it was attacked by ISIS,

00:03:38.300 --> 00:03:39.889
which killed an estimated one

00:03:39.890 --> 00:03:41.869
hundred and seventy civilians and

00:03:41.870 --> 00:03:43.219
13 U.S. soldiers.

00:03:44.240 --> 00:03:46.519
I saw airplanes

00:03:46.520 --> 00:03:48.349
in the ditch. I saw airplanes on

00:03:48.350 --> 00:03:50.089
their sides. I saw helicopters

00:03:50.090 --> 00:03:51.049
completely destroyed.

00:03:51.050 --> 00:03:52.639
I saw that the terminal of the

00:03:52.640 --> 00:03:54.709
airport completely

00:03:54.710 --> 00:03:55.710
demolished.

00:03:56.570 --> 00:03:58.459
Not everyone who was able to escape

00:03:58.460 --> 00:03:59.449
had worked with the U.S.

00:03:59.450 --> 00:04:01.459
forces and the course of searching

00:04:01.460 --> 00:04:03.079
for his men. Peterson also

00:04:03.080 --> 00:04:04.969
encountered three siblings outside

00:04:04.970 --> 00:04:06.829
the Kabul airport trying to get on

00:04:06.830 --> 00:04:08.689
a plane, and he decided to help

00:04:08.690 --> 00:04:09.589
them.

00:04:09.590 --> 00:04:11.329
They now live in an East Coast city

00:04:11.330 --> 00:04:12.949
and asked that we not reveal their

00:04:12.950 --> 00:04:15.019
names or location.

00:04:15.020 --> 00:04:16.849
They looked distraught, but

00:04:16.850 --> 00:04:17.850
terrified.

00:04:18.620 --> 00:04:20.599
So I kind of took these

00:04:20.600 --> 00:04:22.519
three under my wing and the other

00:04:22.520 --> 00:04:23.520
two that were with them.

00:04:30.890 --> 00:04:31.890
They got special treatment.

00:04:39.660 --> 00:04:41.229
Are you going to go back to

00:04:41.230 --> 00:04:43.319
university as well?

00:04:43.320 --> 00:04:44.320
Are you finished?

00:04:45.270 --> 00:04:47.459
Yes, my university is

00:04:47.460 --> 00:04:47.969
going to finish.

00:04:47.970 --> 00:04:50.159
Yeah, just to my two subjects

00:04:50.160 --> 00:04:51.059
remain.

00:04:51.060 --> 00:04:52.311
Oh, take them online.

00:04:53.420 --> 00:04:54.420
Ok, maybe

00:04:55.320 --> 00:04:57.539
when you get the bottom,

00:04:57.540 --> 00:04:59.029
I want to get a copy of.

00:05:00.250 --> 00:05:01.839
When he got back to the U.S.,

00:05:01.840 --> 00:05:03.279
Peterson connected with a growing

00:05:03.280 --> 00:05:05.139
community of volunteers also

00:05:05.140 --> 00:05:06.399
committed to doing whatever they

00:05:06.400 --> 00:05:08.259
could to help stranded Afghans.

00:05:09.760 --> 00:05:11.649
Zach Van Meter, a venture capitalist

00:05:11.650 --> 00:05:13.359
from Florida, rented a conference

00:05:13.360 --> 00:05:14.889
room at the Willard Hotel in

00:05:14.890 --> 00:05:16.629
Washington, D.C., in August to

00:05:16.630 --> 00:05:18.369
coordinate a private volunteer

00:05:18.370 --> 00:05:20.379
effort to get people out.

00:05:20.380 --> 00:05:22.989
It was the Peacock Lounge,

00:05:22.990 --> 00:05:25.059
which I'm not sure what it's exactly

00:05:25.060 --> 00:05:26.259
used for, but it is a

00:05:27.280 --> 00:05:29.289
couple of thousand square foot space

00:05:29.290 --> 00:05:30.969
in the back of the hotel, next to

00:05:30.970 --> 00:05:32.379
the restrooms and away from

00:05:32.380 --> 00:05:33.399
everybody.

00:05:33.400 --> 00:05:36.009
And we set up tables and

00:05:36.010 --> 00:05:38.259
there were anywhere from 40

00:05:38.260 --> 00:05:40.089
to 60 people working in there

00:05:40.090 --> 00:05:42.069
for a week straight people sleeping

00:05:42.070 --> 00:05:43.149
on the ground.

00:05:43.150 --> 00:05:44.709
They convinced the United Arab

00:05:44.710 --> 00:05:46.569
Emirates government to help with the

00:05:46.570 --> 00:05:48.699
evacuation effort, and it assisted

00:05:48.700 --> 00:05:51.699
in getting out 13,000 Afghans.

00:05:51.700 --> 00:05:53.439
Very, very first flight out was a

00:05:53.440 --> 00:05:55.329
young lady and her family who

00:05:55.330 --> 00:05:56.469
had been directly threatened by the

00:05:56.470 --> 00:05:57.999
Taliban, and it was kind of a test

00:05:58.000 --> 00:05:58.959
for us.

00:05:58.960 --> 00:06:01.329
And they went in, they got her,

00:06:01.330 --> 00:06:02.649
they walked her through the airport.

00:06:02.650 --> 00:06:04.989
They put her on a UAE

00:06:04.990 --> 00:06:07.659
military plane like a C-130.

00:06:07.660 --> 00:06:09.009
It was pretty neat moment.

00:06:09.010 --> 00:06:10.869
And so they flew over, and then

00:06:10.870 --> 00:06:13.359
the UAE said, Let's do more.

00:06:13.360 --> 00:06:14.769
Private entities and the U.S.

00:06:14.770 --> 00:06:15.999
government together worked to

00:06:16.000 --> 00:06:18.729
airlift out nearly 130,000

00:06:18.730 --> 00:06:19.569
people.

00:06:19.570 --> 00:06:21.459
Most are now living in camps in the

00:06:21.460 --> 00:06:23.139
United States and other parts of the

00:06:23.140 --> 00:06:24.879
world, awaiting a lengthy vetting

00:06:24.880 --> 00:06:25.989
process.

00:06:25.990 --> 00:06:27.609
Tens of thousands are still in

00:06:27.610 --> 00:06:28.839
hiding.

00:06:28.840 --> 00:06:30.849
You guys are maintaining safe

00:06:30.850 --> 00:06:33.189
homes inside Afghanistan.

00:06:33.190 --> 00:06:34.079
Tell me how that works.

00:06:34.080 --> 00:06:36.159
So we keep the rent paid.

00:06:36.160 --> 00:06:37.299
We keep them warm.

00:06:37.300 --> 00:06:38.319
We try to keep them from getting

00:06:38.320 --> 00:06:40.149
bored. We'll send

00:06:40.150 --> 00:06:41.469
coloring books for kids.

00:06:41.470 --> 00:06:42.669
Try to find activities.

00:06:44.030 --> 00:06:45.789
You know, we keep food going, and

00:06:45.790 --> 00:06:47.799
that's a constant struggle.

00:06:47.800 --> 00:06:49.599
Ben Owen is the founder of Flanders

00:06:49.600 --> 00:06:51.699
Fields, a nonprofit that helps

00:06:51.700 --> 00:06:53.649
resettle refugees inside the U.S.

00:06:53.650 --> 00:06:55.209
and maintains a network of safe

00:06:55.210 --> 00:06:56.199
homes.

00:06:56.200 --> 00:06:57.018
We are trying to provide and I don't

00:06:57.019 --> 00:06:58.719
know how long we can continue to

00:06:58.720 --> 00:06:59.439
provide.

00:06:59.440 --> 00:07:01.779
Flanders Fields is part of a network

00:07:01.780 --> 00:07:03.639
of nonprofits that maintain

00:07:03.640 --> 00:07:06.399
60 safe homes in Afghanistan.

00:07:06.400 --> 00:07:08.979
Aoun's says he has taken out $23,000

00:07:08.980 --> 00:07:10.569
in personal loans to cover their

00:07:10.570 --> 00:07:11.979
expenses.

00:07:11.980 --> 00:07:13.759
How much does it cost you?

00:07:13.760 --> 00:07:15.339
You know, roughly daily to keep

00:07:15.340 --> 00:07:17.199
these safe homes going.

00:07:17.200 --> 00:07:18.819
We go broke literally every single

00:07:18.820 --> 00:07:20.649
day, so some days we spend 10

00:07:20.650 --> 00:07:22.539
grand, some days we spend 20 grand

00:07:22.540 --> 00:07:24.219
Sundays or spend 300 bucks.

00:07:24.220 --> 00:07:25.749
It's it's all dependent on what

00:07:25.750 --> 00:07:27.189
we're able to raise.

00:07:27.190 --> 00:07:29.199
Although the Biden administration is

00:07:29.200 --> 00:07:30.879
currently doing little to help with

00:07:30.880 --> 00:07:32.739
the evacuation efforts, there are

00:07:32.740 --> 00:07:34.339
many individuals within the U.S.

00:07:34.340 --> 00:07:36.189
government who works directly with

00:07:36.190 --> 00:07:38.049
some of the stranded Afghans and

00:07:38.050 --> 00:07:39.969
are helping with private evacuation

00:07:39.970 --> 00:07:41.319
efforts.

00:07:41.320 --> 00:07:42.969
We have a mutual friend who

00:07:42.970 --> 00:07:44.859
literally is taking some

00:07:44.860 --> 00:07:46.839
of his government salary

00:07:46.840 --> 00:07:48.669
to send money so people have food.

00:07:48.670 --> 00:07:50.049
He's never met them before.

00:07:50.050 --> 00:07:51.879
And then there's a lot of people who

00:07:51.880 --> 00:07:54.069
don't want to

00:07:54.070 --> 00:07:56.109
be in the press because they still

00:07:56.110 --> 00:07:57.999
work in a place where

00:07:58.000 --> 00:07:59.169
they're not supposed to.

00:07:59.170 --> 00:08:00.429
The guys that are pushing me to do

00:08:00.430 --> 00:08:01.419
this interview because they don't

00:08:01.420 --> 00:08:03.339
want to do it. They worked while

00:08:03.340 --> 00:08:04.629
on maternity leave.

00:08:04.630 --> 00:08:07.209
They worked while on vacation.

00:08:07.210 --> 00:08:08.859
The Afghans stuck in the country

00:08:08.860 --> 00:08:09.749
face a Catch 22.

00:08:09.750 --> 00:08:11.769
To qualify

00:08:11.770 --> 00:08:13.539
for a special immigrant visa to

00:08:13.540 --> 00:08:14.349
leave.

00:08:14.350 --> 00:08:16.119
They must sit for an in-person

00:08:16.120 --> 00:08:17.319
interview. But the U.S.

00:08:17.320 --> 00:08:19.119
doesn't conduct in-person interviews

00:08:19.120 --> 00:08:20.350
inside Afghanistan

00:08:21.370 --> 00:08:22.749
Because we can't fly them straight

00:08:22.750 --> 00:08:25.809
from Afghanistan to America

00:08:25.810 --> 00:08:28.089
unless it's on a department of state

00:08:28.090 --> 00:08:30.219
flight or some sort of trip

00:08:30.220 --> 00:08:31.179
sponsored by the Department of

00:08:31.180 --> 00:08:32.319
State.

00:08:32.320 --> 00:08:34.209
Josh Jenkins is an army veteran

00:08:34.210 --> 00:08:35.798
who served in Afghanistan for eight

00:08:35.799 --> 00:08:37.329
years. Now he works for the

00:08:37.330 --> 00:08:39.189
nonprofit Ampilo, which uses

00:08:39.190 --> 00:08:41.319
technology to fight poverty and

00:08:41.320 --> 00:08:42.969
is now helping with the evacuation

00:08:42.970 --> 00:08:43.658
efforts.

00:08:43.659 --> 00:08:45.729
We have no way of getting people

00:08:45.730 --> 00:08:47.559
across unless we have a third

00:08:47.560 --> 00:08:49.059
party willing to take them while

00:08:49.060 --> 00:08:51.369
they wait for their SIV or P1

00:08:51.370 --> 00:08:53.799
or P2 or parole applications

00:08:53.800 --> 00:08:55.689
to be approved, or we just send them

00:08:55.690 --> 00:08:56.769
to a different country that's

00:08:56.770 --> 00:08:58.210
willing to accept them instead.

00:08:59.379 --> 00:09:01.539
Owen, Jenkins and 15 other nonprofit

00:09:01.540 --> 00:09:03.699
organizations joined a federation

00:09:03.700 --> 00:09:05.889
started by Travis Peterson called

00:09:05.890 --> 00:09:07.899
Moral Compass. The alliance

00:09:07.900 --> 00:09:09.759
seeks to better coordinate all

00:09:09.760 --> 00:09:11.409
of their funding, logistics,

00:09:11.410 --> 00:09:13.329
advocacy and food programs

00:09:13.330 --> 00:09:15.009
by putting them all under one

00:09:15.010 --> 00:09:16.010
umbrella

00:09:16.779 --> 00:09:17.709
With moral compass.

00:09:17.710 --> 00:09:20.979
We have these 15 organizations,

00:09:20.980 --> 00:09:23.139
and then we have an advocacy

00:09:23.140 --> 00:09:24.759
organization. On top of that, The

00:09:24.760 --> 00:09:26.139
Umbrella, which is the Special

00:09:26.140 --> 00:09:28.539
Operations Association of America.

00:09:28.540 --> 00:09:30.009
The federation, which relies

00:09:30.010 --> 00:09:32.079
exclusively on private donations,

00:09:32.080 --> 00:09:33.969
is exploring new strategies

00:09:33.970 --> 00:09:36.069
to help more Afghans escape, such

00:09:36.070 --> 00:09:37.179
as attempting to build a

00:09:37.180 --> 00:09:39.549
humanitarian village in Kosovo.

00:09:39.550 --> 00:09:41.379
A private citizen had donated

00:09:41.380 --> 00:09:43.269
17,000 square meters of his

00:09:43.270 --> 00:09:45.249
land to us to

00:09:45.250 --> 00:09:46.929
build a humanitarian city.

00:09:46.930 --> 00:09:49.539
We had doctors, lawyers.

00:09:49.540 --> 00:09:51.489
Everything from the top to bottom

00:09:51.490 --> 00:09:53.619
was covered in

00:09:53.620 --> 00:09:55.569
volunteers willing to just come out

00:09:55.570 --> 00:09:56.949
and volunteer their time to help

00:09:56.950 --> 00:09:58.629
these people, and they had no

00:09:58.630 --> 00:10:00.799
expectations of being paid,

00:10:00.800 --> 00:10:02.389
Jenkins says the cost of our

00:10:02.390 --> 00:10:04.309
government said it would sign off if

00:10:04.310 --> 00:10:06.139
the US State Department agreed to

00:10:06.140 --> 00:10:07.909
issue an unobjection certificate,

00:10:07.910 --> 00:10:09.979
establishing that it does not oppose

00:10:09.980 --> 00:10:10.999
the plan.

00:10:11.000 --> 00:10:12.739
It refused.

00:10:12.740 --> 00:10:14.119
Why should these guys?

00:10:14.120 --> 00:10:16.549
Why should your guys qualify

00:10:16.550 --> 00:10:18.709
for a special immigrant visa?

00:10:18.710 --> 00:10:20.149
We made a promise to these people,

00:10:20.150 --> 00:10:21.529
and if we want people to keep taking

00:10:21.530 --> 00:10:22.850
us seriously in the future,

00:10:24.080 --> 00:10:25.549
we need to follow through on that.

00:10:26.690 --> 00:10:28.579
Thousands of Afghans are stuck in

00:10:28.580 --> 00:10:29.989
vetting stations on U.S.

00:10:29.990 --> 00:10:31.879
bases inside the US and around the

00:10:31.880 --> 00:10:33.589
world. They have been awaiting

00:10:33.590 --> 00:10:35.546
processing for over six months now.

00:10:36.560 --> 00:10:38.299
If rejected, some will end up

00:10:38.300 --> 00:10:39.229
stateless.

00:10:39.230 --> 00:10:41.479
There are around 14,000 permanent

00:10:41.480 --> 00:10:43.729
residents and 400 American citizens

00:10:43.730 --> 00:10:45.679
still stuck in Afghanistan who have

00:10:45.680 --> 00:10:47.569
no pathway to immigrate or

00:10:47.570 --> 00:10:48.709
are unwilling to leave their

00:10:48.710 --> 00:10:50.089
families behind.

00:10:50.090 --> 00:10:52.009
During a press conference, Secretary

00:10:52.010 --> 00:10:53.869
Blinken felt like it was important

00:10:53.870 --> 00:10:55.489
to clarify that the American

00:10:55.490 --> 00:10:57.589
citizens will remain in Afghanistan

00:10:57.590 --> 00:10:59.179
carry dual citizenship.

00:10:59.180 --> 00:11:00.439
Most of the remaining American

00:11:00.440 --> 00:11:02.929
citizens are dual nationals

00:11:02.930 --> 00:11:05.239
whose home is Afghanistan

00:11:05.240 --> 00:11:06.589
and whose extended families live

00:11:06.590 --> 00:11:09.139
there. So it's no surprise

00:11:09.140 --> 00:11:10.489
that deciding whether or not to

00:11:10.490 --> 00:11:12.379
leave the place they call home

00:11:12.380 --> 00:11:13.790
is a wrenching decision.

00:11:15.420 --> 00:11:16.999
I've got a woman, an American

00:11:17.000 --> 00:11:19.249
citizen in Missouri

00:11:19.250 --> 00:11:20.719
who has two daughters with her one's

00:11:20.720 --> 00:11:22.729
20 and one's 23.

00:11:22.730 --> 00:11:24.019
U.S. Department of State told her,

00:11:24.020 --> 00:11:25.609
yes, you're an American citizen, you

00:11:25.610 --> 00:11:26.599
can bring your daughter because

00:11:26.600 --> 00:11:28.189
they're both unmarried. Oh wait, one

00:11:28.190 --> 00:11:29.629
is 23. She can't come.

00:11:29.630 --> 00:11:30.979
She's got to stay.

00:11:30.980 --> 00:11:32.869
What mother is going to leave her 23

00:11:32.870 --> 00:11:34.129
year-old, gorgeous daughter in

00:11:34.130 --> 00:11:36.169
Afghanistan by herself

00:11:36.170 --> 00:11:37.369
to give you an answer as to why I

00:11:37.370 --> 00:11:38.419
think it is?

00:11:38.420 --> 00:11:40.969
I have no fucking clue.

00:11:40.970 --> 00:11:42.529
So the problem is it's bigger than

00:11:42.530 --> 00:11:44.689
just us not letting people into

00:11:44.690 --> 00:11:46.349
the US or not bringing people to the

00:11:46.350 --> 00:11:46.939
U.S.

00:11:46.940 --> 00:11:48.169
Noor you're not going to find a

00:11:48.170 --> 00:11:49.849
smoking gun. There isn't a person

00:11:49.850 --> 00:11:51.349
holding this up.

00:11:51.350 --> 00:11:53.179
There isn't a,

00:11:53.180 --> 00:11:54.589
you know, I mean, you can say the

00:11:54.590 --> 00:11:55.909
buck stops here and it's all the

00:11:55.910 --> 00:11:57.169
president's fault, but it's really

00:11:57.170 --> 00:11:57.979
not.

00:11:57.980 --> 00:12:00.679
There's literally a legal structure

00:12:00.680 --> 00:12:02.119
that's been established for how

00:12:02.120 --> 00:12:03.499
immigrants are allowed into this

00:12:03.500 --> 00:12:04.399
country.

00:12:04.400 --> 00:12:06.229
From when my ancestors came into

00:12:06.230 --> 00:12:07.909
your, you came in.

00:12:07.910 --> 00:12:10.129
That's part of the process.

00:12:10.130 --> 00:12:11.869
Then compound that with the fact

00:12:11.870 --> 00:12:12.829
that it's a country on the other

00:12:12.830 --> 00:12:14.629
side of the world and you literally

00:12:14.630 --> 00:12:16.609
need to hop them somewhere.

00:12:16.610 --> 00:12:18.439
Or we need to

00:12:18.440 --> 00:12:20.869
open up our camps

00:12:20.870 --> 00:12:22.819
and, you know, stadiums in house,

00:12:22.820 --> 00:12:25.189
hundreds of thousands of Afghanis

00:12:25.190 --> 00:12:26.899
and just be prepared for that.

00:12:26.900 --> 00:12:28.399
But I don't think our general

00:12:28.400 --> 00:12:30.349
population wants that.

00:12:30.350 --> 00:12:32.149
The Biden administration not only

00:12:32.150 --> 00:12:34.279
oversaw the disastrous withdrawal.

00:12:34.280 --> 00:12:36.379
It also has continued to enforce

00:12:36.380 --> 00:12:38.209
and defend a broken immigration

00:12:38.210 --> 00:12:39.349
system.

00:12:39.350 --> 00:12:41.389
In 2021, it admitted

00:12:41.390 --> 00:12:43.639
only 18 percent of the refugees

00:12:43.640 --> 00:12:45.469
allowed under its self-imposed

00:12:45.470 --> 00:12:46.369
cap.

00:12:46.370 --> 00:12:48.139
The Biden administration has a new

00:12:48.140 --> 00:12:50.269
program that will evacuate roughly

00:12:50.270 --> 00:12:52.309
600 Afghans per week, but

00:12:52.310 --> 00:12:54.769
there are an estimated 100,000

00:12:54.770 --> 00:12:55.770
who qualify for SIV status,

00:12:56.810 --> 00:12:58.549
which means the evacuations could

00:12:58.550 --> 00:13:00.119
take years to complete and they'll

00:13:00.120 --> 00:13:01.459
still have to go through vetting

00:13:01.460 --> 00:13:03.439
facilities already backlogged with

00:13:03.440 --> 00:13:04.879
thousands of unprocessed

00:13:04.880 --> 00:13:05.880
obligations.

00:13:06.770 --> 00:13:07.909
So a lot of people got left in the

00:13:07.910 --> 00:13:08.899
lurch. There were people that

00:13:08.900 --> 00:13:10.159
applied for SIV, maybe four or five

00:13:10.160 --> 00:13:11.119
years ago. They were still waiting

00:13:11.120 --> 00:13:12.529
on their interview.

00:13:12.530 --> 00:13:14.539
So that process needs to be

00:13:14.540 --> 00:13:16.369
modified or changed.

00:13:16.370 --> 00:13:18.049
I understand that Congress is

00:13:18.050 --> 00:13:19.309
looking at ways to do virtual

00:13:19.310 --> 00:13:21.049
interviews and other things.

00:13:21.050 --> 00:13:22.789
We're going to be a joke if every

00:13:22.790 --> 00:13:24.049
time we ask someone to help us,

00:13:24.050 --> 00:13:25.099
they're going to say no. Remember

00:13:25.100 --> 00:13:26.899
Afghanistan? Not only did you lose,

00:13:26.900 --> 00:13:29.049
but you left everyone behind.

00:13:29.050 --> 00:13:30.379
And it's not going to get us

00:13:30.380 --> 00:13:31.939
anywhere. We need to come through

00:13:31.940 --> 00:13:33.769
and actually do what we said

00:13:33.770 --> 00:13:34.699
we do.

00:13:34.700 --> 00:13:36.079
They did everything that we've asked

00:13:36.080 --> 00:13:38.199
them to do over the years, and

00:13:38.200 --> 00:13:39.320
we need to be able to do

00:13:40.970 --> 00:13:42.769
what we told them we would do and

00:13:42.770 --> 00:13:45.259
honor that promise of

00:13:45.260 --> 00:13:46.260
taking care of them.

00:13:47.240 --> 00:13:48.889
They fought to the death, every one

00:13:48.890 --> 00:13:49.890
of them,

00:13:50.750 --> 00:13:51.750
and they're still fighting.

